      a: "Yes. Enter the full market value of your property under Real Estate and the outstanding mortgage under Loans & Liabilities. Neptoon calculates your net housing wealth by considering both values."
    },
    {
      q: "What is the difference between a mortgage and a bank loan?",
      a: "A mortgage is linked to your property and is settled when that property is sold. A bank loan is modeled independently and can represent a housing-related loan, a personal loan or other borrowing. Both have their own interest rates and repayment assumptions."
    },
    {
      q: "Can I include a bank loan used for consumption?",
      a: "Yes. The bank loan can represent borrowing for purposes other than housing, such as a car or personal consumption. You enter the outstanding debt, interest rate and repayment terms, and Neptoon includes the future financing costs."
    },
    {
      q: "Does Neptoon include monthly loan repayments?",
      a: "Yes. Neptoon calculates interest and principal repayments according to each loan's terms. These payments are financed through your Free Portfolio during both BUILDING and USING, and are already included in your Life Cycle results."
    },
    {
      q: "Should I include loan repayments in my monthly savings or consumption?",
      a: "No. Monthly savings represent contributions to your Free Portfolio, while your future consumption target represents your desired lifestyle spending. Mortgage and bank-loan payments are calculated separately, so including them again would double-count the same payments."
    },
    {
      q: "What happens to my mortgage when I sell my home?",
      a: "Any outstanding mortgage is repaid from the property's sale proceeds, together with any applicable deferred property tax. Only the remaining net amount is transferred to your Free Portfolio. The property and associated mortgage are then removed from your Balance Sheet."
    },
    {
      q: "What happens to my bank loan if I sell my home?",
      a: "The bank loan is independent of the property's liquidation in Neptoon. Selling your home does not automatically repay it. The bank loan continues according to its own repayment schedule, even if the borrowing was originally related to your home."
    },
    {
      q: "Why does Neptoon include deferred taxes as liabilities?",
      a: "Some assets have taxes that have not yet been paid. Neptoon recognizes these estimated obligations in your Balance Sheet before settlement, so your economic wealth reflects both the asset value and the associated future tax obligation."
    },
    {
      q: "Does repaying debt make me wealthier?",
      a: "Repaying loan principal reduces your debt but also reduces your Free Portfolio by the same amount. The repayment itself therefore does not create new economic wealth. Interest payments, however, are a real financing cost that reduces your wealth."
    }
  ]
}
